# Accepting & Purchasing Your Offer

We've sent you a link to your private offer. Follow these steps to accept it and get started.

## Step 1: Accept the Offer

1. Open the link we sent you — it will take you to your offer in the Azure Marketplace
2. Review the details: what's included, the pricing, and the start/end dates
3. If there are terms & conditions attached, review them (you can download the PDF)
4. Click **Accept private offer**

> After accepting, the next step (Purchase) may take **15–60 minutes** to become available. You can refresh the page to check.

## Step 2: Purchase

1. When the **Purchase** button becomes active, click it
2. You'll be asked to select an **Azure subscription** and **resource group** — if unsure, ask your Azure administrator which to use
3. You'll be asked to name the purchase (e.g. "Normain <plan name>") — this is just a label for your own reference
4. Set **auto-renew** to **off** (we will help you with renewal when the time comes)
5. Click **Review + subscribe** → **Subscribe**
6. Wait for it to finish setting up

> If the Purchase button is greyed out, hover over it — a message will explain why. The most common reason is that it's not ready yet (wait a bit and refresh).

## Step 3: Activate the Subscription

1. When the subscription is ready, you'll be redirected to our website (or shown a link to it). Follow the instructions on the page to confirm and activate your subscription. **Your purchase is not complete until you do this.**
2. Once the subscription is successfully set up, you'll be automatically redirected to the sign-in page (see Step 4 below)

## Step 4: Sign In to the Application

1. If you were not automatically redirected, go to the application link we sent you (`<your-instance>.normain.com`)
2. Sign in with your Microsoft work email
3. The first time you sign in, Microsoft will ask you to approve our app. Depending on your organization's settings:
   - **You may be able to approve it yourself** — just click **Accept**
   - **You may need IT approval** — click **Request approval** and your IT department will receive a request to approve the app. Once they do, you can sign in again

> **Note for your IT department**: The approval request appears in the Microsoft admin center under **Enterprise applications** → **Admin consent requests**. It's a standard sign-in permission — it lets our app verify your identity. No data beyond your basic profile (name and email) is accessed.

## Need Help?

If you get stuck at any point, reach out to us and we'll help you through it.
